<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's 1996 cotton imports fall 6.2 pct on yr.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's 1996 cotton imports fall 6.2 pct on yr.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's cotton imports fell 6.2 percent to 346,000 tonnes in 1996 from 369,000 tonnes a year earlier, an official at the Spinners and Weavers Association of Korea said on Friday.  </p>
<p>The association official attributed the fall in the country's cotton imports to high labour cost and downsizing of the industry.</p>
<p>&quot;This year's imports are also expected to go down, though we can not forecast the numbers now,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>He said the United States supplied about 45 percent of the total, followed by the states that belonged to former Soviet Union with 34 percent and Australia with seven percent.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
